# Phase 18 MessageExt queue-offset override follow-up — 2026-10-21T18:31:56Z

Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
Code revision: `a5bfd35b` (`feat(common): preserve MessageExt subtype queue offsets`)
Pinned Java source: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.
Fixture SHA-256: `00a09f96bb75f96f2ae81111e83c916af4dc47999b7462efdb82163ab8e1fe54`.

## Source audit and change

- Java `ProcessQueue.putMessage` indexes messages by virtual
  `MessageExt.getQueueOffset`; its setter is also overridable. Rust previously
  read and wrote the stored base offset directly.
- Added optional `getQueueOffset`/`setQueueOffset` hooks to
  `MessageExtSubtype`. Rust queue insertion/removal now observes the subtype's
  virtual offset accessor through the existing `MessageExt::queue_offset` API.
- Extended the invoked Java custom subtype fixture to record the virtual
  offset and setter call. A Java `ProcessQueue.putMessage` run is compared with
  Rust for the dispatch flag, tree key, message count, body size and setter
  count. All 27 direct-consume cases and the direct ProcessQueue comparison
  pass.
- Updated the Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 crosswalks and release checklist.
  Other inherited virtual methods remain part of the broader audit.

